W276 R26 -- the ONLY change to the recompiler's INPUT that closes the 0x00577168 dispatch miss.
The authoritative engine TOML lives on the SSD (it names generated output paths), so this patch is
what keeps the fix from surviving only on one disk. Addresses and config only -- no game bytes.

Apply to w251-engine_authoritative.toml (the engine recompilation config):
  1. add the "hook_577168@0x00577168" entry_points line + its comment (hunk 1)
  2. point output at the r26 emit directory (hunk 2) -- for the run that produced
     /mnt/ssd/vulcan4-build/recomp_engine_r26/, 47 objects, harness relinked 2026-10-08 19:54:04

Verified at the emit: register_functions.cpp slot 1170520 =
  g_ps2EngineFunctionTable[1170520] = sub_00577100_0x577100; // 0x577168
and ps2_recompiled_functions_40.cpp carries `case 0x577168u: goto label_577168;` + `label_577168:`.
Verified at the boot: run/boot_w276r26.log and boot_w276r26b.log, halt=wallclock_deadline,
missing_functions=0, no JALR missing-target line (pre-fix boot_w276r26c.log halted at elapsed_ms=6256
with `no generated function at this pc pc=0x00577168`).

=== hunk 1: bak-r26 -> authoritative (the fix)
--- w251-engine_authoritative.toml.bak-r26	2026-10-08 19:34:29.789269732 +0300
+++ w251-engine_authoritative.toml	2026-10-08 19:35:57.926376251 +0300
@@ -166,6 +166,19 @@
 # Guest functions without runtime handlers that may be referenced by address.
 # PS2Recomp keeps their guest implementation and exposes exact callable entries.
 entry_points = [
+  # R26: Ghidra's function list (engine-symbols.csv) has a HOLE at 0x577168. It is a real
+  # 8-byte guest function -- 0x577168 jr $ra / 0x57716c addiu v0,$zero,1 -- reached only
+  # through a RUNTIME-BUILT pointer table (s0=0x617d98, s0[0]=0x577168), so no static call
+  # reference exists, so it is neither a known function start nor an interior of any
+  # function that itself holds an unresolved indirect jump -- and the W236 fallback only
+  # promotes interiors of the function that CONTAINS the unresolved jump
+  # (control_flow_analyzer.cpp:442, addr >= function.start && addr < function.end), never
+  # the jump's target in a different function. NOT the NO_FALLBACKS knob: it is measurably
+  # unset here (register_functions.cpp has the caller's own interior 0x5773e4 at slot
+  # 1170679). Measured halt in run/boot_w276r26c.log: no generated function at pc=0x00577168.
+  # discoverAdditionalEntryPoints() turns this into a resume entry under its owner
+  # (0x577100) -- the same shape as the already-registered neighbour 0x577170.
+  "hook_577168@0x00577168",
   "handler_5B73C8@0x005B73C8",
   "handler_5B7390@0x005B7390",
   "handler_5B7408@0x005B7408",
=== hunk 2: authoritative -> w276-engine_r26 (the emit dir for the verified run)
--- w251-engine_authoritative.toml	2026-10-08 19:35:57.926376251 +0300
+++ w276-engine_r26.toml	2026-10-08 19:36:08.947147641 +0300
@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@
 ghidra_output = ""
 
 # Path to output directory
-output = "/mnt/ssd/vulcan4-build/recomp_engine_w251/"
+output = "/mnt/ssd/vulcan4-build/recomp_engine_r26/"
 
 # Single file output mode (recommended for large games)
 single_file_output = true
